==Finnish==

===Etymology===
{{root|fi|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-}}
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*konëh}}, from Pre-Finnic ''*konïš'', borrowed from Pre-{{der|fi|gem}} ''*gn̥ni̯o-'' (later {{cog|gem-pro|*kunją||omen, portent, miracle}}), from {{der|fi|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-}}. Cognates include {{cog|non|kyn||wonder}}. The original meaning in Finnish was "magic, magic trick".<ref>Kallio, Petri: [http://www.sgr.fi/sust/sust266/sust266_kallio.pdf The Prehistoric Germanic Loanword Strata in Finnic]</ref> The development of senses attested in the written language is "means, method" (1725), "tool" (1734), "apparatus, instrument" (1745), "machine" (1770s).<ref>{{R:fi:NSES}}</ref> Cognate with {{cog|krl|koneh||magic}}, {{m|krl|konehtie||to conjure}} and {{cog|et|kõne||speech}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|*}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[machine]] {{gloss|mechanical or electrical device}}
# [[appliance]] {{gloss|apparatus or device, typically powered electrically, used in homes to perform domestic functions}}
#: {{uxi|fi|[[kodinkone|kodin'''kone''']] / [[kotitalouskone|kotitalous'''kone''']]|[[household appliance|household '''appliance''']]}}
# {{n-g|Short for various compound words ending in {{m|fi|kone}}.}}
